# Dashboard-local ignores.
#
# Until Phase E this whole directory was hidden by a single `/dashboard` line in
# the repository .gitignore. That one line was doing all the work, so removing
# it to commit exposed three artifact trees that no other rule catches. The
# rules below are deliberately duplicated with the root file: this directory
# should stay safe to commit even if the root rules are edited.

# Dependencies.
node_modules/

# Build output.
#
# `dist/` alone is not enough. The root file's `**/dist` matches a path
# component named exactly `dist`, so `dist-scorecard/` slips straight past it.
dist/
dist-scorecard/
dist-studio/

# Wrangler local state. Never commit.
#
# The root file's `/.wrangler` is root-anchored and does not reach the copies
# nested under web/ and studio/. What they hold is not build junk:
#
#   - `cache/cf.json` records the developer's city, region, postal code and
#     latitude/longitude to five decimal places, plus ISP and ASN.
#   - `tmp/` retains bundled worker sources and sourcemaps, including the
#     Basic Auth worker DEPLOY.md describes as removed, and roughly forty
#     absolute `C:\Users\...` paths.
.wrangler/

# Vite's dependency-optimiser scratch space.
.vite/
.vite-temp/
